[rexglue-native] SDK 0302, released in setup tool 2.26.0 (2026-11-03; owner 05:46 "sync release", answer
"Native set, opt-in"). Native resolves (Vulkan), only with native_render_targets on (0301): a resolve goes
straight from the host render target into guest memory (a compute pass writes the tiled bytes the EDRAM
path would have) and into the texture made from that memory (color by vkCmdCopyImage, depth k_24_8 and
k_24_8_FLOAT converted through a scratch buffer), so that texture isn't loaded again. Anything that
doesn't fit goes the old way. Off, nothing changes.

This file is three drafts folded into one diff (applies after 0301):
  0302    native resolves                    drafts/0302-native-resolves.UNTESTED.patch            5d0b28ee
  0302 r2 native resolve counters (census)   drafts/0302-r2-native-copy-counters.UNTESTED.patch     ea56e0fb
  0302 r3 depth resolves into textures       drafts/0302-r3-depth-into-textures.UNTESTED.patch      55822af0
The diff is git's diff between the tree with 0300 + 0301 and the tree with all three applied
(rexglue-native/rel/0302-folded.diff, md5 4f12d37b); the drafts' own text is in dev/agents/rexglue-native/.

Tested by rexglue-native-test on the owner's PC (2026-11-02/03): 4-player split screen on 6 MP maps,
native against the emulation: texture loads 0 MB a frame (41 MB), the same cost per draw on the GPU
emulation thread, which still limits 4-player frame rates, and pictures the same
(dev/agents/rexglue-native/N3-BENCH-4P-r3.md, FINDINGS-0302-r3.md); graphics card time 6.44 against
7.12 ms a frame in an mp_merv profile (NR8-PROFILE-SUBMITS-CARD.md). The exact release set
(fork + 0001-0149 + 0300-0302) built and run 2026-11-03 (dev/agents/rexglue-native/RELEASE-2.26.0.md).

